te truth  okay  i'm saying not just  about what others will say in the sense  that what your neighbors or your friends  will say i'm even saying this with  respect to your own brothers and sisters  even to your own parents  okay  do not worry about what others including  all these people will say  ultimately it is just a game between you  and the james the examination questions  okay  and  uh you realize as as you grow older you  will realize that  this kinds of thoughts which especially  comes up and which seems to dominate  your entire psyche especially in your  teenage years as you grow older you will  realize that you are probably  overestimating  the kind of thoughts people have about  you  okay so they think actually much less  about you than you actually think that  they think about you okay so this is a  bunch of words but i hope i make myself  clear  so everyone has their own problems  everyone has their own struggles  they may think about you a little bit  but  in all likelihood you are overestimating  how much they are thinking about you  okay so  just like you do not spend your entire  day thinking about others they are also  not thinking about you so you don't have  to worry on that account and  at the end of the day even if for  argument's sake let's say they are  thinking  what can you do about it it is not in  your hand so why bother okay so take a  very philosophical stand about it the  other negative thought very obvious very  evident that will naturally come to your  mind is that  if you do not perform well what will  happen to your future  well  the philosophical stand to take here is  that at this moment just before the  examination this is not the time to  think about it  okay you will have ample time to think  over it to ruminate over it to  to torture yourself as much as you want  later on after the results are out so  why bother now  right now your entire aim should be to  extract the most out of the preparation  that you have whatever little  preparation you have try to extract the  most out of it this is the crux of the  mental game  okay so  you will see that  many people who may not or or rather  many people who have exactly the same  level of preparation that you have may  be able to perform better than you have  just because they are able to push out  all these kinds of negative thoughts out  of their brain and then  perform absolutely to the best of their  abilities and to the absolute best 100  percent of the potential of their  preparation so you also try try to do  that  the next thing is not  a negative thought but this als  almost always happens especially with  people who are taking who are attending  a big examination like j means for the  first time  because of all the media hype and all  the youtube videos  that they see  it creates  a some sort of a  perverted picture in their mind  regarding the apparent importance of  such an examination they put it up on a  very high pedestal they respect it like  anything they worship the j means so  this kind of an attitude like too much  respect for an examination is actually  detrimental to your ability to actually  perform well in that examination rather  your attitude should be  slightly irreverent okay irreverent  attitude towards the examination i'm not  saying to disrespect it but if you  respect it way too much you will not be  able to perform well with it you'll not  be able to  play it like a game  uh  and  give your best  okay so i hope you uh you understand  what i'm trying to say the next thing  is that  many of you may be thinking  that  if you can somehow get into iit life is  set  nothing can be farther from the truth  okay there are  examples of many students who come to  iit think like that that their life is  set then they goof off take it way too  easy  and then their entire life is ruined  this has happened to many many students  what you should be thinking is that the  opportunity  to study at iit  is not a license is not a privilege to  take it easy and to have musty all the  time of course there will be moments of  fun  like in every college there will be  moments of fun but in but the  opportunity to study in an iit  or in any good institute is actually  what it is really is an opportunity  for you to struggle even more to fight  even harder to get  better results to improve your academic  credentials to uh to go higher and  higher it is an opportunity to fight  even more it is not an opportunity to  just have fun and to goof off  so these are some of the mental things  which i think we should keep in mind  uh in these last few days  but  the most important tip that i have  shared with you i think is that you  should not put it up on a pedestal  worship it  rather play it like a game and you you  see that you will be able to extract the  best out of your preparation no matter  how it is now  so with that with these things i will  just end this video all the very very  best

